{"id": "EUVD-2026-86741", "enisaUuid": "6f394a7c-82ed-3d1a-93ed-6a4a63da70a5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix uninitialized return value in netfs_unbuffered_write()\n\nIf preparation of the first subrequest fails,\nnetfs_unbuffered_write() exits its loop before ret is initialized. The\nempty-iterator check can do the same.\n\nFor synchronous writes, netfs_unbuffered_write_iter_locked() may then\nreturn an unrelated error instead of wreq->error. This is reachable\nthrough CIFS if cifs_prepare_write() fails to reopen the file or obtain\ncredits.\n\nInitialize ret to 0 so the caller returns wreq->error if no data was\nwritten, or the number of bytes already written otherwise.\n\nFound with Clang's -Wconditional-uninitialized.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d038eebdbd400c3bc4b66bd8aa0dff0c2bcce26", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2e38d500471d097cda87d7d374bbc1b13493075d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f18e8774f4d3137fa0a5fb8ffa83d59a719666d8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97610", "GHSA-x5p7-qjx7-h5j9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17019726-7b85-328e-86e1-1c7be509399b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a0b4c7a49137ed21279f354eb59f49ddae8dffc2 <2e38d500471d097cda87d7d374bbc1b13493075d"}, {"id": "3d0b63a0-4530-31c4-85da-3e560b1a3906", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.17 <6.18.53"}, {"id": "3e8a7035-ce0c-3191-8a75-e853cae586c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "5434824e-c937-3c87-a81b-9fd360fe7666", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5edca403-bb78-38eb-b608-7e685334ddc0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19.7 <6.20"}, {"id": "783dcad0-abdd-3187-a3fe-71695a7da1b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "72d08d2839649d1c5efbe375751f4473fa4486af <3d038eebdbd400c3bc4b66bd8aa0dff0c2bcce26"}, {"id": "868a0552-14c9-3359-9736-8b0787986004", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "900c4c64-b761-35c9-86f3-1bea8b63aeb1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "e6733b99-bce4-3cb9-88f5-4cc863650d23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0c29f6d63122a0168d67cb8ecde5b4cf7fe4acb0"}, {"id": "e749c895-24cb-34d0-9280-c78818a91dee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "f75f6903-de97-3f88-a253-3886779d9001", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a0b4c7a49137ed21279f354eb59f49ddae8dffc2 <f18e8774f4d3137fa0a5fb8ffa83d59a719666d8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ffc10926-cc19-3622-a043-2f30efc043cf", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}